spans.s:
moṣaka, m.
(1) (Skt. and [mosaka] Pali Lex., see Childers; = Skt. moṣa), robbing; a robber: udyāna-˚kāḥ puruṣāḥ Divy 〔175.12, 15〕; ayaṃ cauro rājakula-˚ko Mv 〔ii.167.18〕 (prose; here perh. specifying -ka), this is the thief that has been robbing the palace;
(2) (= Skt. moṣa) plunder, stolen goods: MSV 〔iv.62.2, 5〕; 〔63.7 ff.〕
